    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yo, i'm looking at a 2022 f150 in the shop. transmission is slipping bad. i'm seeing some weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit on the scan tool. what are the most likely culprits for pressure fluctuations like that? i wanna narrow down if its a solenoid issue or something else before i start tearing into the valve body.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes often point to solenoid issues, such as a sticking, leaking, or failing pressure control solenoid. However, it could also indicate problems within the torque converter or internal valve body passages if cavitation or restricted flow is occurring. Before removing components, checking the fluid level and cleanliness is crucial, as contaminants can cause erratic pressure readings.",
      "source": "target",
