    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'll try the solenoid swap first. one more thing though—sometimes with these newer ford units, they just act up for no reason, like something is just messing with the electronics or the hydraulic flow. do you ever see cases where it's just some random, intermittent glitch that drives you crazy because you can't find a physical cause?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, frustrating intermittent electrical glitches, often related to poor ground connections, wire harness chafing, or an Environmental Control Unit (ECU) communication fault, are surprisingly common. These phantom issues are notoriously difficult because the error disappears the moment you try to test for it, mimicking a mechanical problem. Thorough electrical tracing and checking for corrosion or moisture ingress into connectors are essential steps when physical components seem fine.",
      "source": "target",
